"THE DDL AS CANON. engine/rust emits CREATE TABLE text inside op_sql_project (main.rs 10827 and 10949, two forms); canon carried system:sqlname/sqlcol_base/sqlcol -- the naming half -- but no emitter at all, and that absence is what blocked deleting those lines rather than any doubt about whether they belonged here. ddl._q's ruling stands and is why every identifier is quoted: the base metamodel projects tables named constraint, transition and view, which are SQL reserved words. A column spec is <name,type,refs> where refs is the empty string or a REFERENCES clause, so ONE arm serves both the plain and the foreign-key column instead of the two branches the Rust carries. keycols empty means the key rode in on a column's own type (TEXT PRIMARY KEY -- the entity form); keycols non-empty means the trailing PRIMARY KEY clause (the relation form).",
"strdown is chardown lifted to a string -- ALPHA over chars, imploded. chardown came into canon with the char family; nothing had lifted it, so engine/rust still owned to_ascii_lowercase. Note the emptiness test below is eq against the empty string, NOT null: null asks whether a value is phi, and an empty STRING is an atom, never phi -- null of it answers F.",
