"quote_str is the JSON spelling of a string, and it is sl:slug's construction again -- chars, a per-character COND, implode -- which is the third time that shape has retired a boundary op (slug, render:json_seq, now this). The escape table is four rows because JSON needs no more for the atoms this store carries: backslash and quote double, newline and return take their letter forms. The literals survive the polyglot embedding because all five host grammars read the same escapes: A(chr(92)) is one backslash to CPython, rustc, javac, Roslyn and bun alike, and canon already relies on this for the newline in main:report_text. quote_str bottoms on a non-string exactly as before -- not by a guard here, but because chars is strict and a bottom operand poisons the fold (Backus 11.2.1: a sequence with bottom as an element IS bottom).",

"strip_prefix is POLICY-FREE, and that is the whole reason it can be canon: the parity ledger's 2026-07-08 ruling is `<prefix, s> -> tail-or-s, policy-free', so at pre == s the tail is the empty string and NO guard trims it. The js head carried a `t.length > pre.length' guard once, every station was transliterated from it, and identical siblings cannot disagree about their common ancestor -- the four engine kernels never had it, which is how the split was finally seen. Written here the guard cannot come back: take n and compare, drop n or answer the operand. Character arithmetic only, over chars / theta:take / theta:drop / implode, so an empty prefix takes phi, compares equal, drops nothing, and a prefix longer than the operand takes fewer characters, compares unequal, and answers the operand -- the three edges the guard used to get wrong.",

